-- Selah database baseline.
--
-- One migration for the whole schema. It replaced migrations 0000-0052 on
-- 2026-10-23, before anything was deployed; a database built from it is the
-- same, object by object, as one built from those (git history has them).
-- Every later change is a new migration after this one.
--
-- Part 1: enums, tables, keys and indexes, generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/db/schema. Part 2: the rules drizzle-kit can't express: functions,
-- triggers, row-level security, grants and reference rows, in sections named
-- after the migrations they came from.
--
-- Bodies refer to functions defined further down, so they are checked when
-- they run rather than when they are created (check_function_bodies).

-- ==========================================================================
-- Part 1: tables (generated by drizzle-kit)
-- ==========================================================================
